WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.302 size:81% position:41%
-Guys, it is important
to remember there are

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.203 line:92%
two sides to every news story.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:06.506
To make sure you get to see
important issues from all sides,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have invited
two of our writers

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have very different
points of view.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.177 line:92%
We will examine their opinions

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:14.080 size:81% position:41%
in a segment we call
"Point, Counterpoint."

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.316 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.686 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:23.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ally, Amber,
thanks for being here today.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.024 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
First topic.

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
President Trump
temporarily ended

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:29.029
the longest government shutdown
in U.S. history on Friday

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:29.829 line:92%
without even getting his wall.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:33.266
Is it worth shutting it down in
two weeks for him to try again?

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ally?
-Absolutely not.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
It will throw this country
into turmoil.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:38.438 line:92%
How is it not illegal for him

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:41.374
to use the livelihood of all
these Americans as leverage

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.877
for him to get a stupid monument
to himself?

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A monument to himself.
Amber?

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:50.917
-If I had a monument of myself,
it would be so cool!

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:53.553 size:78% position:39%
It would be just like
the Lincoln Memorial,

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:56.122 line:92%
except I'd be sitting like this.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:02.962
As the plaque would say
"She sure did like margaritas."

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Another great point.
Next topic.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
BuzzFeed reported
President Trump directed

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
his lawyer, Michael Cohen,
to commit perjury,

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
and although
Robert Mueller's team

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.706
said that wasn't quite accurate,
they didn't refute it, either.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:17.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
Too early to throw around
the word "impeachment"? Ally?

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.678 line:92%
-No, because this is literally

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the reasons
Nixon was impeached.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.148 line:92%
And we all know Trump did it.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
The only thing I worry about
is that right now

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
our alternative
is human robot Mike Pence.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.888 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Human robot. Amber?

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Robotic voice ]
I am a human robot.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.094 line:92%
I know how to walk, how to talk.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:37.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
But no one ever taught me
how to love.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ] Hey, remember
how data from "Star Trek"

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
was always like,
"I wish I was real"?

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would always be like,
"How do you have

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
all these strong feelings
when you're a robot?

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.743 line:92%
Something doesn't add up."

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.179 size:88% position:44%
-Seth, what she's saying
is completely off topic.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ally, it's called
"Point, Counterpoint."

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:59.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
She makes a point,
you make a counterpoint.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.821 line:92%
-We're all doing a good job!

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.889 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Next topic.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
The field of Democrats
running for President in 2020

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
grows by the day,
but this could also mean

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.395 size:81% position:41%
another vicious battle
to become the nominee.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:13.199
Can the Democrats survive their
own primary season? Ally?

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.567 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Honestly, who knows?

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.203
People already have their
claws out on social media.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just don't get
why these people

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.373 line:92%
want to destroy their own party.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Destroy their own party.
Amber?

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:25.378
-♪♪ It's my party,
I'll destroy it if I want to ♪♪

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.848
♪♪ Destroy it if I want to,
destroy it if I want to ♪♪

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.918
-Those aren't the words!
-♪♪ And you would do it, too ♪♪

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.486 line:92%
♪♪ Flappy flippy dee floo ♪♪

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:36.556 size:84% position:42%
♪♪ Ba ba beep boop bop,
ah ba ba ba ba ba ♪♪

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.258 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Next topic, please!

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.994
-Finally, the Chinese government
has arrested a scientist

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.428 line:92%
they say gene-edited two babies.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.030 size:88% position:44%
Should be this illegal,
or could it help parents

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
protect their future children
from disease? Ally.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Helpful or not, once
governments gets their hands

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
on this technology,
it will be bad news.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.373 size:81% position:41%
As it is, I refuse to
give my DNA to 23andMe

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they're just
going to sell it.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:58.244
We need a president who will
pass legislation on this soon.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Maybe I'll run for president.
-[ Laughs ] Okay.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, if you were serious
about being president,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.985 line:92%
you'd announce it formally.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.353 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-All right.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Where's she going?
-I don't know.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.792 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:13.593 line:92%
-Good evening from New York.

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:19.065
Our top story tonight is about
migrating tree frogs that --

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:20.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Can I help you?

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.467 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Hi. I'm Amber Ruffin.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:25.471
And I'm running for
President of the United States!

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:29.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh...great.
What's your platform?

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:34.113 line:92%
-Margaritas for everyone!

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.415 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I don't hate it.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.418 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Okay, bye! Love you!

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.420 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Love you, too?

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.056 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.290 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There you go.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.025 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.860 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.963 line:92%
-I can't believe you did it.

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:52.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't believe
you didn't do it on this show.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:56.736 size:84% position:42%
-Oh. Is that something
other people are doing?

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.605 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:00.773 line:92%
But it'd be cool if they did.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, then.
I'm running for President!

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, shut up, Ally.
-Fair.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This has been
"Point, Counterpoint."

